        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Stole pieced together from a silk having a wide chiné stripe in the centre in white and pink, flanked by narrow stripes in pale blues, wider stripes in plain yellow and a fancy stripe of spaced salmon-pink stripes on creamy-white silk.\n\nThe ends are trimmed with a narrow gold lace. At each end and in the centre is a cross of gold braid woven from gold thread, gilt metal strip in two widths and cream silk. \n\nThe stole is stiffened with white linen and lined with pink silk."@en , "Stole of chiné silk, France, 18th century"@en ;
